{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 28, :comments ["<b>And His spirit.</b> The spirit that goes forth from His mouth, by way of parable concerning the angel:" "<b>To sway.</b> Most of the commentators say that להנפה is like להניף (to wave), and R. Moses the Kohen said that it is like רסן (a bridle), and behold, this spirit is like the lying spirit that was prophesied concerning by Micah (1 Kings 22:19), and this is the correct view, and the reason is that a bridle is placed on the jaws of a horse to lead it on the straight path, but this spirit places a misleading bridle. And like it: <b>with vanity to sway.</b> And the meaning of להנפה is like קשר (a bond)."], :book :isaiah, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 30, :notes {1 "The final sentence comparing להנפה to קשר is textually difficult; translated hyper-literally."}, :source-witnesses [["Ibn Ezra on Isaiah, by M. Friedlander; Society of Hebrew Literature, London 1877" "https://www.nli.org.il/he/books/NNL_ALEPH001338443"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T18:56:07.458445093Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}